      <activity id="5a7f8112-a425-53d2-a75b-3b3add91722d" activityNameId="a87143cb-48ae-5e83-80c9-a834319fd3ba" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Stibnite ore, 70% stibnite, at mine</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Stibnite ore, 70% stibnite, at mine
The model represents mining and beneficiation of Stibnite in China. China produces more than 80% of the global Antimony.;
Formula: Sb2S3; 
UUID: 4212afbd-7ef5-35ff-b6d8-9be0aebd1a5f
The module includes the mining and the beneficiation step with the mining infrastructure and disposal of overburden and tailings (see part "Auxiliary Processes").
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: This module is approximated with values from molybdenum mining and beneficiation (coupled with copper mining)
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_4212afbd-7ef5-35ff-b6d8-9be0aebd1a5f.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
